## Testing

Run the test suite:

```bash
python -m pytest -q
```

---

## Benchmarks

Performance is tracked continuously with [CodSpeed](https://codspeed.io). The benchmark suite lives in
`benchmarks/` and covers the hash primitives, secp256k1 scalar multiplication, address encoding for every
supported family, Base58/WIF conversions, ECDSA signing and recovery, BIP39/BIP32 derivation, and address
validation.

Run the benchmarks as plain tests to check they still behave correctly:

```bash
python -m pip install pytest-codspeed
python -m pytest benchmarks/ -q
```

Measure them locally with the CodSpeed CPU simulation instrument:

```bash
codspeed run --mode simulation -- python -m pytest benchmarks/ --codspeed
```

Every merge request runs the same command in CI, so performance changes are reported before they are merged.

